# Database

Columns are `snake_case`, TypeScript is `camelCase`, and the mapping is
explicit at the column. Tenant-scoped tables lead with `organization_id`.

## Migrations are generated, never hand-written

```bash
pnpm db:generate   # after editing schema.ts
pnpm db:migrate    # apply
```

Do not edit a file in `migrations/` that has already been committed, and never
edit `migrations/meta/`. Drizzle tracks state in those snapshots, and a chain
that disagrees with the SQL beside it fails in ways that are hard to read. To
undo something, change `schema.ts` and generate a new migration.

Check what was generated before committing it. `ADD COLUMN ... NOT NULL` on a
table that already has rows will fail on any database that is not empty; that
needs a nullable column, a backfill, and a follow-up migration.

## Better Auth owns four tables plus three more

`user`, `session`, `account`, `verification`, and — from the organization
plugin — `organization`, `member`, `invitation`. Their field names and
nullability come from the plugin's own schema. Diverging produces adapter
errors at runtime, not at build time, so copy from the plugin rather than
guessing.

## The pool assumes a long-running server

`max: 10` per process. On serverless, every warm instance holds its own pool —
put a pooler in front rather than raising the number.
